  fit: {mode: fill}
notes: |
  Timing: about 35 seconds.

  I want to begin with a question: where am I standing when I look at a painting? My project began with Velázquez's Las Meninas, but it eventually connected a seventeenth-century room, a worn charging cable, my own drawing, a small convolutional autoencoder, and a four-second moving image. The common thread is the position of the viewer—how a work of art can make that position visible, and how a neural network reveals a very different kind of looking.
